course: dictionary
lesson: 15157
title: Scope: range, chance and room
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Scope has a few meanings, so the words around it tell you which one you need. Its main meaning is the range of things a subject, job or plan deals with. «The project's scope is the history of our town, not its future.» The clue is project and history: scope means what the project includes.
explain: «There is scope for improvement in your spelling.» Here scope means chance or room to do something. Try swapping in room: «There is room for improvement in your spelling.» It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: «That question is beyond the scope of this lesson» means it is outside what the lesson covers. «Let's scope out the new park before we go in» is informal and means look carefully to check it. Read the words around scope, then pick the meaning that fits.
fact: Scope means the range of things that a subject, job or plan deals with.
fact: Scope can also mean a chance or opportunity, as in «There is scope for improvement.»
fact: «Beyond the scope» means outside what is covered.
fact: Informally, scope is short for telescope, microscope or the sight on a rifle, and «scope out» means to look carefully at something to check it.
exercise: «The science club's scope covers plants, rocks and weather.» In this sentence, scope means what? | *The range of things the club deals with | A chance to win a prize | A tiny lens for seeing germs | A cup for drinks
exercise: «Your story has scope for a surprise ending.» What does scope mean here? | A sharp view through a rifle | A type of boat | *A chance or room to do something | The area a map covers
exercise: Ben says, «Let's scope out the new climbing wall before we start.» What does scope out mean? | Ignore it completely | Race to the top | *Look carefully to check it | Paint it green
test: «The lesson is beyond the scope of our course, so we won't study it.» What does beyond the scope mean? | Too easy for the class | *Outside what the course covers | Far away from school | Inside the course, in the middle
test: Maya uses a microscope and says, «I need the scope to see the cells.» In this sentence, scope is short for what? | A paint brush | A football pitch | A school bag | *A microscope
exam: Which sentence uses scope to mean the range of things a job deals with? | «There is scope for a bigger garden.» | «Please scope the room for a good seat.» | *«Her job's scope covers checking trains and signals.»
